<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Delaware Colony</h1><p class="st-meta">1664 CE – 1776 CE · capital New Castle</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Lower Counties on the Delaware, a former Swedish and Dutch settlement area that shared Pennsylvania's governor but kept its own assembly and became the first state.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwaanendael">Zwaanendael</a> near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lewes-delaware">Lewes</a> was destroyed in 1631, and in 1638 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-sweden">New Sweden</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-christina">Fort Christina</a> at what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilmington-delaware">Wilmington</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-netherland">New Netherland</a> conquered the Swedish colony in 1655, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-casimir">Fort Casimir</a>, renamed New Amstel, later became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-castle-delaware">New Castle</a>. After the English conquest of 1664 the area was ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-england">James, Duke of York</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 1682 James granted the three counties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-castle-delaware">New Castle</a>, Kent and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-sussex">Sussex</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-penn">William Penn</a>, who governed them with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-pennsylvania">Province of Pennsylvania</a>. The Lower Counties resented domination by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a> and from 1704 met in their own assembly at New Castle, while still sharing the Penn family's governor. Farmers of Swedish, Finnish, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and English descent grew grain and tobacco, and enslaved Africans worked many farms in the south.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 15 June 1776 the assembly declared the Lower Counties separate from both <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesar-rodney">Caesar Rodney's</a> ride helped carry the vote for independence. As the state of Delaware, it was the first to ratify the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">United States Constitution</a> in 1787.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/delaware-colony.jpg" alt="Delaware Colony" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: AnonMoos, based on image by Zscout370, AnonMoos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_ensign_of_Great_Britain_(1707%E2%80%931800,_square_canton).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1664 CE – 1776 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>New Castle</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William Penn, John Penn, Caesar Rodney</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lower Counties on the Delaware</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1720&amp;focus=delaware-colony" aria-label="Delaware Colony on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2816 757 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Delaware Colony lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3136 1013L3186 980M3136 1013L3186 980M3136 1013L3149 1004M3136 1013L2570 1008"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3186 980h0M3186 980h0M3149 1004h0M2570 1008h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3136 1013h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3136 1013h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks New Castle. <a href="/atlas?year=1720&amp;focus=delaware-colony">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
